-- Passage rg8-word-parts-p03
insert into public.passages (id, code, skill_id, sat_alignment, grade_band, title, body, status)
values ('9e7ac8f4-6e05-5e57-bdee-e604ea847a07', 'rg8-word-parts-p03', (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g8-word-parts'), null,
        '6-8', $q$Halftime Adjustments$q$, $q$Amara's soccer team was losing 2 to 0 at halftime, and the bench was silent. The other team's goalkeeper had rejected every shot, swatting the ball away as if she could predict where it would go.

Coach Bertrand gathered the players under the shade of the bleachers. Instead of shouting, he pulled out a small whiteboard and drew a diagram of the field. "Their defenders are crowding the middle," he said, tapping the board. "We keep sending the ball straight into traffic. Let's use the sidelines."

Amara studied the diagram. Her role was to run along the left edge of the field and project the ball across toward the goal, where her teammate Hoang would be waiting.

The second half began, and the plan worked almost at once. Amara sprinted down the sideline and sent a high pass toward the center. Hoang headed it into the corner of the net. The crowd erupted in cheers so loud that Amara could barely hear the referee's whistle.

With ten minutes left, the score was tied. Then a defender's shoe split along the side, and the referee stopped play while she changed it. The short delay gave everyone on Amara's team a chance to catch their breath.

On the final play, Amara faked a pass, then cut inside and shot. The goalkeeper dove, but the ball was already past her.

After the game, Coach Bertrand erased the whiteboard. "Good adjustments," he said. "Same plan next week."$q$, 'draft')
