insert into public.passages (id, code, skill_id, sat_alignment, grade_band, title, body, status)
values ('873d0846-6a26-5ef2-8825-d99f8b2550f5', 'rg8-word-parts-p04', (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g8-word-parts'), null,
        '6-8', $q$The Footbridge on Mill Creek$q$, $q$For years, students who lived on the east side of Mill Creek had a long walk to school. The only crossing was a road bridge with a narrow shoulder, and parents worried about the trucks that transported gravel from the nearby quarry.

Last year, the town council voted to construct a footbridge just for walkers and cyclists. The project was expensive, but a local benefactor, a retired engineer named Rosalind Achebe, donated a large share of the money. She asked only that the bridge be finished before the school year began.

Workers imported steel beams from a mill in another state because no local supplier made them long enough. A crane lifted each beam into place while a small group of neighbors watched from the bank.

The builders also thought about people with different needs. The ramps on both ends have a gentle slope, so the bridge is easy to use for people in wheelchairs. Small speakers at each end play an audible tone when the crossing signal at the road changes, which helps people who cannot see the light.

On opening day, students crossed the bridge in a steady stream. A sign near the entrance thanks Ms. Achebe and lists the year of construction. Most students walk past it without reading it, but they all use the bridge she helped build.$q$, 'draft')
