   $q$The Greek root seismo means "shake," and graph means "write" or "record." What is a "seismograph"?$q$, $q$[{"text":"A device that records the shaking of the ground","is_correct":true},{"text":"A map that shows where faults are located","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"too-narrow"},{"text":"A device that stops the ground from shaking","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"ignores-second-root"},{"text":"A tool that warns people before an earthquake","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$A device that records the shaking of the ground$q$, $q$Seismo plus graph means "shake record," and the passage says it "records those waves." It cannot warn people ahead of time, since the passage says no scientist can yet say when a major earthquake will occur.$q$, 'draft', 'b719150c-a79f-551e-8685-73bfe4a7b64e')
