   $q$The Greek root bio means "life," and degrade means "break down." What does "biodegradable" mean in the passage?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Able to grow into a new living plant from seed","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"ignores-second-root"},{"text":"Able to stay in the soil for years unchanged","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"opposite-meaning"},{"text":"Able to be used again many times without harm","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"confuses-similar-word"},{"text":"Able to be broken down naturally by living things","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Able to be broken down naturally by living things$q$, $q$Bio plus degradable means "able to be broken down by life," which is why peels rot into soil. Staying in the soil for years is what the passage says happens to plastic, which is not biodegradable.$q$, 'draft', '8847c7c5-aef2-59f7-93b5-2d357de8bddb')
