   $q$The Latin prefix mal- means "bad" or "badly." What happened when the thermometer began "to malfunction"?$q$, $q$[{"text":"It needed to be cleaned of compost.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"context-only-guess"},{"text":"It started working faster than before.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"opposite-meaning"},{"text":"It stopped working the way it should.","is_correct":true},{"text":"It showed a very low temperature.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"too-narrow"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$It stopped working the way it should.$q$, $q$Mal plus function means "work badly," and the thermometer "showed the same reading no matter what." The passage never says the reading was low, only that it never changed.$q$, 'draft', '8847c7c5-aef2-59f7-93b5-2d357de8bddb')
