   $q$The prefix contra- means "against," and the root dict means "say." What did Ingrid do when she "contradicted" Darius?$q$, $q$[{"text":"She broke in before he finished speaking.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"confuses-similar-word"},{"text":"She repeated his words back to the teacher.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"ignores-first-root"},{"text":"She agreed with what he said about the smell.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"opposite-meaning"},{"text":"She said the opposite of what he claimed.","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$She said the opposite of what he claimed.$q$, $q$Contra plus dict means "say against," and Ingrid argued the pile "should smell like a forest floor" when Darius expected a terrible smell. Breaking in while someone talks is interrupting, which uses the root rupt instead.$q$, 'draft', '8847c7c5-aef2-59f7-93b5-2d357de8bddb')
