   $q$The Latin root aqua means "water," and duct means "lead." What is an "aqueduct"?$q$, $q$[{"text":"A large pool where people in the city went to swim","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"ignores-second-root"},{"text":"A stone arch built to hold up the roof of a building","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"too-narrow"},{"text":"A channel built to lead water from one place to another","is_correct":true},{"text":"A pump that pushes water uphill to the city fountains","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$A channel built to lead water from one place to another$q$, $q$Aqua plus duct means "water leader," and the passage calls it "a long channel that carried water." It was not a pump, since the passage says the system "relied on gravity rather than pumps."$q$, 'draft', 'e4c35e27-2411-507c-936d-39049ee24786')
